.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
something that can be automatically moved, spun or resized over time\&. 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBAnimated\fP separates immediate edits and constant rates from scheduled transitions\&. All animation durations and waits use floating-point seconds\&. Setters are immediate and chainable; they cannot consume a \fBwait()\fP or \fBandThen()\fP\&. Timed change methods require explicit seconds; explicit zero applies immediately outside a sequence\&. To names specify targets; By names specify additive deltas\&. \fBgrow()\fP and \fBstretch()\fP use factors and change logical size; \fBchangeScaleTo()\fP/changeScaleBy() change the independent transform scale\&. Constant rates continue after a rate transition ends\&.

.PP
Scheduled operations normally run concurrently\&. \fBandThen()\fP sequences the next operation after the most recently scheduled one; \fBwait()\fP delays the next timed request\&. Immediate calls after either throw before changing state\&. \fBcancelSchedule()\fP clears pending sequencing and scheduled work while retaining current constant rates\&.

.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
sprite\&.setMovement(40, 0);
sprite\&.changeMovementTo(0, 0, 0\&.5); // Ease the rate to a stop in half a second\&.
sprite\&.setGrowing(8);             // Add eight logical size units per second\&.
sprite\&.changeGrowingTo(0, 0\&.25);  // Ease the growth rate to zero\&.

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBPhysicsBody\fP owns physical velocity, mass, damping, forces and impulses\&.

.PP
It has no drawing capabilities, so it is not intended to be used directly in most cases, but rather as a base class for items that can be animated\&. It could be used on a server to drive animation that is rendered on the client\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSprite\fP 

.PP
\fBSpriteLayer\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "\fBAnimated\fP addAnimationHelper (\fBIAnimationHelper\fP helper)"

.PP
Register a callback after the object's normal animation step\&. The callback runs as \fRcallback\&.call(helper, owner, deltaSeconds)\fP and returns a boolean: true keeps its registration, false retires it\&. Helpers run in registration order\&. Adding the same helper twice to one owner has no effect; a helper may also be registered on several owners\&. A retained helper can be added again after it finishes\&.

.PP
Callbacks may remove themselves, remove another helper, or clear the owner's helpers\&. Removed callbacks do not run later in the same step\&. Additions first run on the next step\&. Removing and re-adding the current helper creates a new registration, which is unaffected by the old callback returning false\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIhelper\fP An \fBIAnimationHelper\fP constructed from a callback\&. Active registrations retain it\&. After retirement, normal JavaScript references determine its lifetime\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The original owner object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const helper = new pdg\&.IAnimationHelper(function(owner, deltaSeconds) {
    owner\&.rotateBy(deltaSeconds * 0\&.5);
    return true;
});
sprite\&.addAnimationHelper(helper)\&.setMovement(20, 0);
// Later: sprite\&.removeAnimationHelper(helper);

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBremoveAnimationHelper()\fP, \fBclearAnimationHelpers()\fP, \fBIAnimationHelper\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBAnimated\fP andThen ()"

.PP
Start the next timed operation after the most recently scheduled operation finishes\&. Uses its remaining duration and delay, not the longest of all concurrent operations\&. The next request consumes this sequencing state; later calls again run concurrently unless sequenced\&. A successor acquires its properties and resolves relative targets when it starts\&. Immediate calls after \fBandThen()\fP throw even if the predecessor has finished\&. No then() method is provided, so returning an \fBAnimated\fP object from an async JavaScript function is safe\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwait()\fP, \fBcancelSchedule()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean animate (number deltaSeconds)"

.PP
Advance programmed animation by elapsed seconds\&. Advances constant rates, scheduled animations and helpers\&. MVC controllers advance their Views automatically\&. Standalone \fBAnimatedAttributes\fP instances must be advanced explicitly; \fBDrawing\fP copies \fBAttributes\fP samples\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdeltaSeconds\fP Finite nonnegative elapsed seconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if any animation value changed\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBpauseSchedule()\fP, \fBaddAnimationHelper()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBAnimated\fP cancelSchedule ()"

.PP
Discard scheduled animations and pending sequencing\&. Keeps current values, constant rates and the paused state\&. Clears pending \fBwait()\fP/andThen() state\&. \fBAnimatedAttributes\fP also clears appearance and frame transitions\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBhasScheduledAnimations()\fP, \fBpauseSchedule()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBAnimated\fP changeCenterOffsetBy (number x, number y, number durationSeconds, int easing = \fR\fBeaseInOutQuad\fP\fP)"

.PP
Animate the rotation-center offset by a delta\&. Adds to the pivot offset\&. With \fBandThen()\fP, the delta is applied to the offset when the operation starts\&. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds\&. Zero applies immediately; a request after \fBwait()\fP or \fBandThen()\fP must have positive duration\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIx\fP Relative pivot delta in the owning object coordinate system\&. 
.br
\fIy\fP Relative pivot delta in the owning object coordinate system\&. 
.br
\fIdurationSeconds\fP Finite nonnegative duration in seconds\&. 
.br
\fIeasing\fP Integer easing constant; elapsed time and duration use seconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetCenterOffset()\fP, \fBchangeCenterOffsetTo()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::easeInOutQuad\fP\&.
