.SS "\fBAnimated\fP changeGrowingBy (number amountPerSecond, number durationSeconds, int easing = \fR\fBlinearTween\fP\fP)"

.PP
Animate the growing rate by an additive delta\&. Uses logical units per second equally on both axes\&. Duration is the time to reach the new rate, not the lifetime of the motion: the final rate continues until changed or stopped\&. With \fBandThen()\fP, the delta is added to the rate when this operation starts\&. Logical size changes independently of transform scale\&. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds\&. Zero applies immediately; a request after \fBwait()\fP or \fBandThen()\fP must have positive duration\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIamountPerSecond\fP Change in growth rate in logical size units per second\&. 
.br
\fIdurationSeconds\fP Finite nonnegative duration in seconds\&. 
.br
\fIeasing\fP Integer easing constant; elapsed time and duration use seconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetGrowing()\fP, \fBchangeGrowingTo()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
